## 4 Methods

Problem definition. Here we intend to design a specific agentic system for disease-relevant analysis, including disease diagnosis and risk factor (such as gene) prioritization. Our agent system 𝒜\mathcal{A} can take the following information as inputs, including task-specific prompts R​\_​xR\\_x, phenotypes P​\_​xP\\_x, functional and/or genetic information of risked genes GG, and medical record information CC. For the problem of disease diagnosis, this system makes inference with Oi=𝒜​(Rd,Pi,Gi,Ci)O\_{i}=\mathcal{A}(R\_{d},P\_{i},G\_{i},C\_{i}) for the patient ii, and the diagnosis result will be the output. Similarly, for risk gene prioritization, we replace the task-specific prompt RdR\_{d} with RgR\_{g}, and the output will be the prioritized gene. The model output not only contains the expected diseases or genes (in string), but also the confidence of making such a decision ranging from 0-100.

